// =====================================================
// TAAPI v1 -> v2 MIGRATION — what to change in N8N (UI settings + 4 Code nodes)
//
// WHY
//   * The API key on the account is a v2 key (taapi_live_sk_...). The v1 endpoint rejects it
//     ("You are not authenticated to query this endpoint") and no v1 key can be obtained.
//   * v2 has NO 2h timeframe (supported: 1m 5m 15m 1h 4h 1d 1w). The pipeline uses 9 two-hour
//     indicators, so those are computed from Binance 2h candles (same algorithms as TA-Lib,
//     verified against the real TA-Lib). 1h and 15m indicators still come from TAAPI v2.
//   * Result: the fields that Row 3 / Row 4 read (rsi_2h, adx_2h, ema_200_2h, ...) are unchanged.
//
// ROW 2 LOOP BODY — the chain after the change
//
//   Loop Over Items1 -> Cooldown after Batch 6 -> [IF/Wait nodes as before]
//     -> HTTP POST TAAPI BULK            (changed, section 2)
//     -> TAAPI RESPONSE PROCESSOR        (new code,  section 3)
//     -> Binance Klines 2h               (NEW HTTP node, section 4)
//     -> 2H INDICATOR CALCULATOR         (NEW Code node, section 5)
//     -> Final post to DB                (unchanged)
//
// -----------------------------------------------------
// 1. Credential (the API key goes ONLY here — never in a node, never in git)
//   Credentials -> Create -> "Header Auth"
//     Name:         TAAPI v2
//     Header Name:  Authorization
//     Header Value: Bearer <YOUR_V2_KEY>        (the word Bearer, one space, the key; no quotes)
//
// 2. HTTP POST TAAPI BULK
//   Method POST · URL https://v2.taapi.io/bulk
//   Authentication: Generic Credential Type -> Header Auth -> "TAAPI v2"
//   Send Headers: off · Send Query Parameters: off
//   Send Body: on · Body Content Type: JSON · Specify Body: Using JSON
//   JSON (expression):   {{ JSON.stringify({ constructs: $json.constructs }) }}
//   Delete the old body fields ("secret", "construct").
//   Options -> Response -> "Include Response Headers and Status": OFF  (the processor reads the body directly)
//   Settings: Retry On Fail ON (2-3 tries) · On Error: Stop
//   Plan: Pro (3 constructs per request). The request now has 2 constructs (1h, 15m): 11 indicators.
//
// 3. Code "Separation of Requests" and "TAAPI RESPONSE PROCESSOR"
//   Replace the code with row2/Separation of Requests and row2/TAAPI RESPONSE PROCESSOR.
//   Processor mode: Run Once for All Items.
//
// 4. NEW HTTP Request node "Binance Klines 2h" (after TAAPI RESPONSE PROCESSOR)
//   Method GET · URL https://api.binance.com/api/v3/klines          (public, no key; same host as Row 1)
//   Send Query Parameters: on
//       symbol   = {{ $json.symbol }}
//       interval = 2h
//       limit    = 1000
//   Options -> Response -> "Include Response Headers and Status": ON   (item.json = { body: [...], statusCode })
//   Settings: Retry On Fail ON (3 tries, 2000 ms) · On Error: Continue (a failing symbol only loses its 2h fields)
//   Weight: ~5 per request, ~100 per cycle (Binance allows 6000/min).
//
// 5. NEW Code node "2H INDICATOR CALCULATOR" (after Binance Klines 2h)
//   Mode: Run Once for All Items · paste row2/2H INDICATOR CALCULATOR
//   The node names it references MUST be exactly:  TAAPI RESPONSE PROCESSOR
//
// -----------------------------------------------------
// FIRST RUN CHECK
//   a) HTTP POST TAAPI BULK output: keys like BTCUSDT_1h / BTCUSDT_15m with rsi, macd, ... inside.
//   b) TAAPI RESPONSE PROCESSOR log: "SUMMARY: N symbol(s) processed, 0 error response(s)".
//   c) 2H INDICATOR CALCULATOR log: "N symbol(s), N with all 12 two-hour fields".
//      A new listing with < 200 two-hour candles (16 days) lacks ema_200_2h only (logged, never invented).
//   d) Final post to DB receives the same fields as before (rsi_2h, macd_value_2h, ... 26 indicator fields).
//   e) Supabase: select symbol, rsi_2h, adx_2h, ema_200_2h, rsi_1h from scan_results order by created_at desc limit 5;
//      (table name as in your project) — no NULLs in the 2h columns.
//
// CHECK AGAINST TAAPI (once, on your computer) — see tools/validate_2h_vs_taapi.html:
//   run scripts/taapi_v2_validation_command.js -> PowerShell asks TAAPI for the SAME 9 indicators on 1h,
//   paste the result into the page: it recomputes them from Binance candles with the production library
//   and shows the difference per indicator (all rows should say MATCH).
//
// NOTES / LIMITS
//   * Every algorithm was compared with the real TA-Lib (the library behind TAAPI) on 22 random data sets x 6
//     scenarios: agreement ~1e-12. Whether TAAPI's own build behaves identically is what the page above checks.
//   * StochRSI uses TA-Lib STOCHRSI(14, fastK 3, fastD 3) = the parameters of the old v1 2h request.
//   * Tiny prices (e.g. 1e-8): checked against TA-Lib too - RSI stays correct, no special case needed.
//   * The partially formed Binance candle is dropped (= v1 "backtrack: 1": last closed candle).
// =====================================================
